      "writtenOn": "2024-04-02T04:12:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Consider this edge case:\n1. Chrome added FastPair monitor `2c fe` (let\u0027s say scanner 0, handle\u003d0)\n2. An NearbyShare advertisement got reported. We spawn a child monitor for it\n3. Chrome added NearbyShare monitor `2c fe fc 12 8e` (let\u0027s say scanner 1, handle\u003d1)\n4. The same NearbyShare advertisement got reported again with handle\u003d1\n5. Both scanner 0 and 1 could be returned by this `find_map` based on the hashmap iteration order. If 0 is returned, the advertisement got ignored\n\nSo I think here we should first match the handle, and only try to match the address if there\u0027s no matching handle.\n\nBut this also means we would be inserting 2 monitors with exactly the same address. The chipset would probably disallow it though. A proper fix could be \"allowing the address monitor handle to be shared between different scanners\".",
